From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 11:22:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(control): the child was told the wrong terminal size

A ghostty pane told its shell it was 56x18 while being 109x27. `stty size`
disagreed with the pane's own CSI 18 t, long lines wrapped at half the
width, and any full-screen program drew into a box a third of the pane.
Resizing the window corrected it, which is what disguised a pty bug as a
rendering quirk.

ConptyConnection::Resize applies a size to the pseudoconsole only while the
connection is Connected; before that it records the numbers for Start() to
use. But Start() transitions to Connecting, *then* creates the
pseudoconsole, and only reaches Connected afterwards - so a resize arriving
in that window is recorded and applied to nothing.

That window is exactly where ours arrives. TermControl initializes the core
before starting the connection, libghostty sizes its surface during that
initialization, and the resulting resize_pty callback is the one carrying
the real grid. Captured from the app's own trace:

    resizeConnection 56x18 cells        <- ghostty's default grid
    set font-size = 12
    cellSize 14x28 px
    pushSize panel=1024.0x520.0 dips scale=1.500 -> 1536x780 px
    resizeConnection 109x27 cells       <- correct, and lost

The size was computed correctly every time. It never reached the
pseudoconsole.

The core now remembers the last grid size resize_pty asked for and replays
it when the connection reports Connected. Resize is idempotent, so the
replay costs nothing when the size already took.

Verified: `wsl stty size` in a fresh pane answers 27 109, matching the
pane's own CSI 18 t. Before, the same probe answered 18 56.

unitControl 62 passed / 0 failed / 1 skipped.

This has plausibly been wrong since Phase 5 - the phase report records the
first ghostty pane running at 56x18 - and survived because nothing had ever
asked the child how big it thought it was. That check is now manual-
validation step 1b.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp    | 34 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.h      | 10 ++++--
 2 files changed, 42 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
index 75d6b5f78..5a6570182 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
@@ -368,6 +368,34 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
 
     void GhosttyControlCore::_connectionStateChangedHandler()
     {
+        // Re-apply the grid size the moment the pty can receive it.
+        //
+        // ConptyConnection::Resize only reaches the pseudoconsole while the
+        // connection is Connected; before that it just remembers the numbers for
+        // Start() to use. But Start() transitions to Connecting, *then* creates
+        // the pseudoconsole, and only reaches Connected afterwards - so a resize
+        // arriving in that window is recorded and never applied to anything.
+        //
+        // That window is exactly where ours arrives. TermControl initializes the
+        // core before starting the connection, libghostty sizes its surface
+        // during that initialization, and the resulting resize_pty callback is
+        // the one carrying the real grid. The result was a child that spent its
+        // whole life believing the terminal was 56x18 while the pane was 109x27:
+        // `stty size` disagreed with the pane's own CSI 18 t, long lines wrapped
+        // at half the width, and any full-screen program drew into a box a third
+        // of the pane. Resizing the window fixed it, because by then the state
+        // was Connected - which is what made it look like a rendering quirk
+        // rather than a pty bug.
+        //
+        // Resize is idempotent, so replaying it costs nothing when the size
+        // already took.
+        if (_connection && !_closing && _ptyColumns > 0 && _ptyRows > 0 &&
+            _connection.State() == TerminalConnection::ConnectionState::Connected)
+        {
+            _trace(L"reapplying pty size %ux%u on connect", _ptyColumns, _ptyRows);
+            _connection.Resize(_ptyRows, _ptyColumns);
+        }
+
         _raiseOnUiThread([this]() { ConnectionStateChanged.raise(*this, nullptr); });
     }
 
@@ -392,6 +420,12 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
     void GhosttyControlCore::ResizeConnection(uint16_t columns, uint16_t rows) noexcept
     try
     {
+        // Remembered even when there is no connection to tell yet: this is the
+        // authoritative grid size, and _connectionStateChangedHandler replays it
+        // once the pty can actually receive it.
+        _ptyColumns = columns;
+        _ptyRows = rows;
+
         if (!_connection || _closing)
         {
             return;
diff --git a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.h b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.h
index 314370487..dc6432254 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.h
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.h
@@ -276,8 +276,8 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
         void _raiseOnUiThread(std::function<void()> action);
 
         Control::IControlSettings _settings{ nullptr };
-        Control::IControlAppearance _unfocusedAppearance{ nullptr };
-        bool _hasUnfocusedAppearance{ false };
+        Control::IControlAppearance _unfocusedAppearance{ nullptr };
+        bool _hasUnfocusedAppearance{ false };
         void _setUnfocusedAppearance(const IControlAppearance& newAppearance);
         TerminalConnection::ITerminalConnection _connection{ nullptr };
         TerminalConnection::ITerminalConnection::TerminalOutput_revoker _connectionOutputRevoker;
@@ -313,6 +313,12 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
         // terminal is not using.
         winrt::Windows::Foundation::Size _cellSize{ 0, 0 };
 
+        // The grid size libghostty last asked the pty for, re-applied when the
+        // connection reaches Connected. See _connectionStateChangedHandler for
+        // why remembering it is necessary rather than belt-and-braces.
+        uint16_t _ptyColumns{ 0 };
+        uint16_t _ptyRows{ 0 };
+
         // The panel's size in DIPs, as TermControl reports it, kept separately
         // from the pixel size handed to libghostty - see _pushSize().
         float _panelWidth{ 0 };
